Incident-02-Phishing Attack
Inbound Email Containing Suspicious External Link

Overview:
An inbound email containing an external hyperlink triggered a phishing detection alert due to the presence of a domain 
not previously categorized as trusted.


Analyst information:
Analyst Role: SOC Level 1 Analyst (Simulation)
Investigation Environment: TryHackMe Lab Environment
Alert Severity: Medium
Time to Resolve: 7.9 minutes
Investigation Date: 13 May 2026

Email content analysis:
The email welcomed a new employee and requested completion of onboarding setup through an external link:

"https://hrconnex.thm/onboarding/15400654060/j.garcia"

The message appeared to originate from an HR onboarding workflow.


Investigation process:
Alert review
Confirmed alert triggered by external embedded hyperlink.
Medium severity assigned automatically by email security controls.

Sender verification
Checked sender domain: hrconnex.thm
Domain structure consistent with HR onboarding platform naming.
No spoofing indicators detected.
SPF/DKIM tools indicated valid results.


Link analysis:
Inspected URL structure.
No URL shorteners used.
Domain matched sender address.
No suspicious redirects observed.
Link context aligned with onboarding workflow.


Context validation:
Recipient appears to be new employee onboarding target.
Message context logically matches HR onboarding process.
Communication tone professional and expected.


Alert classification: false positive
Legitimate onboarding communication.
Verified sender domain.
No malicious indicators detected.
Business context validated.


Response action taken:
Case closed as false positive.
Email allowed.
Alert reviewed and documented.





